{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-001", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "The drama of life is a psychological one in which we bring circumstances to pass by our attitudes rather than by our acts.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["ATTITUDE"], "tags": ["attitude", "self-concept", "psychology"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-002", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "Man, by assuming the feeling of his wish fulfilled, alters his future in harmony with his assumption, for, assumptions though false, if sustained, will harden into fact.", "primary_topic": "ASSUMPTION", "secondary_topics": ["FEELING"], "tags": ["assumption", "wish-fulfilled", "persistence"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-003", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "When satisfaction is yours, you no longer hunger for it.", "primary_topic": "WISH_FULFILLED", "secondary_topics": ["FEELING"], "tags": ["satisfaction", "desire", "completion"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-004", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "Consciousness is the one and only reality. Therefore, we must form the object of our desire out of our own consciousness.", "primary_topic": "CONSCIOUSNESS", "secondary_topics": ["DESIRE"], "tags": ["consciousness", "desire", "creation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-005", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "The first step in changing the future is Desire, that is, define your objective — know definitely what you want.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["TECHNIQUE"], "tags": ["desire", "objective", "clarity"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-006", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "Experience has taught me to restrict the imaginary action which implies fulfillment of the desire, to condense the idea into a single act, and to re-enact it over and over again until it has the feeling of reality.", "primary_topic": "IMAGINATION", "secondary_topics": ["TECHNIQUE", "FEELING"], "tags": ["imaginal-act", "repetition", "feeling-of-reality"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-007", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 1", "quote_original": "You must, with the minimum of effort permeate the mind with the feeling of the wish fulfilled.", "primary_topic": "WISH_FULFILLED", "secondary_topics": ["EFFORT"], "tags": ["minimum-effort", "feeling", "wish-fulfilled"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-008", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 2", "quote_original": "When you assume the feeling of your wish fulfilled it is with a minimum of effort.", "primary_topic": "WISH_FULFILLED", "secondary_topics": ["EFFORT"], "tags": ["assumption", "minimum-effort", "wish-fulfilled"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-009", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 2", "quote_original": "Just relax and enter into the feeling of actually being what you want to be.", "primary_topic": "FEELING", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["relaxation", "identity", "desire"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-010", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 3", "quote_original": "We can create a new approach to life.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CHANGE"], "tags": ["change", "approach", "life"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-011", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 3", "quote_original": "Things that I am not attentive to fade and wither within my world, regardless of what they are.", "primary_topic": "ATTENTION", "secondary_topics": ["IMAGINATION"], "tags": ["attention", "focus", "withdrawal"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-012", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "There is nothing to change but our concept of self.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CHANGE"], "tags": ["self-concept", "change", "identity"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-013", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "Any enlargement of our concept of Self involves a somewhat painful parting with strongly rooted hereditary conceptions.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CHANGE"], "tags": ["self-concept", "growth", "conditioning"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-014", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "The ideal with which we are united works by association of ideas to awaken a thousand moods to create a drama in keeping with the central idea.", "primary_topic": "IDEAL", "secondary_topics": ["MOOD", "IMAGINATION"], "tags": ["ideal", "mood", "association"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-015", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "Love and hate have a magical transforming power, and we grow through their exercise into the likeness of what we contemplate.", "primary_topic": "ATTENTION", "secondary_topics": ["LOVE"], "tags": ["contemplation", "love", "transformation"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-016", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "To know what you want is the start of prayer.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["PRAYER"], "tags": ["clarity", "prayer", "desire"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-017", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "A single sensation dominates the mind, if you pray successfully.", "primary_topic": "PRAYER", "secondary_topics": ["FEELING"], "tags": ["sensation", "attention", "prayer"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-018", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "What would I feel like, now, were I what I want to be?", "primary_topic": "FEELING", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["feeling", "identity", "question"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-019", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 4", "quote_original": "That which you seek is already housed within you.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["DESIRE"], "tags": ["within", "desire", "identity"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-020", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 5", "quote_original": "Give yourself a new concept of self for the old concept. Give up the old concept completely.", "primary_topic": "SELF_CONCEPT", "secondary_topics": ["CHANGE"], "tags": ["self-concept", "change", "release"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-021", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 5", "quote_original": "The most remarkable feature of man’s future is its flexibility.", "primary_topic": "FUTURE", "secondary_topics": ["IMAGINATION"], "tags": ["future", "flexibility", "choice"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-022", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 5", "quote_original": "The desires which impel us to action are those which hold our attention.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["ATTENTION"], "tags": ["desire", "attention", "action"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-023", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 5", "quote_original": "Attention minus effort is indispensable to changing the future.", "primary_topic": "ATTENTION", "secondary_topics": ["EFFORT"], "tags": ["attention", "effort", "future"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-024", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Lesson 5", "quote_original": "How the waking dream becomes physical fact is not our concern.", "primary_topic": "IMAGINATION", "secondary_topics": ["TECHNIQUE"], "tags": ["waking-dream", "means", "technique"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-025", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Master class Q&A", "quote_original": "The acceptance of the end wills the means.", "primary_topic": "ASSUMPTION", "secondary_topics": ["TECHNIQUE"], "tags": ["end", "means", "acceptance"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-026", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Master class Q&A", "quote_original": "It takes an intense hunger to bring about a transformation of self.", "primary_topic": "DESIRE", "secondary_topics": ["SELF_CONCEPT"], "tags": ["hunger", "transformation", "self-concept"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id": "FL-CUR-027", "corpus_id": "S001", "author": "Neville Goddard", "source_title": "Five Lessons (Master Class)", "source_year": 1948, "source_slug": "five_lessons", "source_section": "Master class Q&A", "quote_original": "The best denial is total indifference. Things wither and die through indifference. They are kept alive through attention.", "primary_topic": "ATTENTION", "secondary_topics": ["REVISION"], "tags": ["indifference", "attention", "release"], "editorial_decision": "SELECT", "review_mode": "SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL", "source_file": "master_text_five_lessons.txt", "review_policy": "EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
